 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a growing pause between attempts: 2, 4, 6 and
+8 seconds.
 
 Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
 can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
 drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
 
+The pause between attempts grew from 3 back-to-back attempts after a Friday when the gateway's status page showed
+slow responses during its 17:00-19:00 peak, and three attempts sent within the same second all landed in that same
+slow window: 58 confirmed pantry orders went uncaptured, and a volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's
+dashboard the next morning. Replaying that Friday's timeouts against the sandbox showed that 5 attempts spaced 2, 4,
+6 and 8 seconds apart would have captured 57 of the 58. Switching gateways was rejected, since the contract runs to
+December 2026. The trade-off accepted is a member who hits a slow capture waits up to 20 seconds longer on the
+confirmation page.
+
